# Accessibility Baseline

Applies to every XingAI public product UI. Target: **WCAG 2.1 AA**.

This is not optional. Accessibility is required for global reach (EU EAA 2025, ADA in the US) and improves usability for all users.

## Semantic HTML First

Use the right element before reaching for ARIA:

```tsx
// ✅ — button is focusable and keyboard-operable by default
<button onClick={handleSubmit}>Analyze</button>

// ❌ — div needs manual tabIndex, role, keydown handler
<div onClick={handleSubmit}>Analyze</div>
```

Use: `<button>`, `<a href>`, `<input>`, `<select>`, `<label>`, `<nav>`, `<main>`, `<header>`, `<footer>`, `<section>`, `<article>`, `<h1>–<h6>`.

## Focus Management

- All interactive elements must be keyboard-reachable (Tab) and activatable (Enter/Space).
- Never use `outline: none` or `outline: 0` without a custom focus ring replacement.
- Modals and drawers must trap focus while open and return focus to the trigger on close.
- On route change, move focus to the new page heading or a skip-link target.

```css
/* Required — never remove this without a replacement */
:focus-visible {
  outline: 2px solid var(--primary);
  outline-offset: 2px;
}
```

## ARIA Rules

Add ARIA only when semantic HTML is not enough:

```tsx
// Dynamic regions that update (AI results, status messages)
<div role="status" aria-live="polite">{statusMessage}</div>

// Error messages
<div role="alert">{errorMessage}</div>

// Icon-only buttons
<button aria-label={tr(lang, "Close menu", "关闭菜单", "메뉴 닫기")}>
  <XIcon aria-hidden="true" />
</button>

// Loading spinners
<div role="status" aria-label={tr(lang, "Loading...", "加载中...", "로딩 중...")}>
  <Spinner aria-hidden="true" />
</div>
```

Rules:
- `aria-label` or `aria-labelledby` on every control without visible text.
- `aria-hidden="true"` on decorative icons and images.
- `aria-expanded` on toggles (menus, accordions).
- `aria-invalid` + `aria-describedby` on form fields with errors.

## Color and Contrast

- Text contrast: minimum **4.5:1** for body text, **3:1** for large text (18px+ regular or 14px+ bold).
- Never use color alone to convey meaning — pair with icon, label, or pattern.
- Test in both light and dark mode.
- Do not rely on placeholder text as a label.

Tools: [contrast.tools](https://contrast.tools), Chrome DevTools contrast checker.

## Images and Media

```tsx
// ✅ informative image
<img src={chart} alt={tr(lang, "Portfolio allocation pie chart", "投资组合饼图", "포트폴리오 파이 차트")} />

// ✅ decorative image
<img src={decorative} alt="" aria-hidden="true" />

// Next.js Image
<Image src={logo} alt="XingAI logo" width={120} height={40} />
```

- Every `<img>` must have `alt`. Decorative images: `alt=""`.
- Videos must have captions for any spoken content.

## Forms

```tsx
// ✅ — label associated with input
<label htmlFor="goal">
  {tr(lang, "Your investment goal", "您的投资目标", "투자 목표")}
</label>
<input
  id="goal"
  type="text"
  aria-required="true"
  aria-describedby={error ? "goal-error" : undefined}
/>
{error && (
  <p id="goal-error" role="alert" className="text-sm text-destructive">
    {error}
  </p>
)}
```

Never use placeholder as the only label for an input.

## Mobile Accessibility

- Touch targets: minimum 44×44 CSS px (applies to both sighted and assistive tech users).
- Do not disable zoom (`user-scalable=no` is banned — fails WCAG 1.4.4).
- Ensure swipe gestures have tap alternatives.

```html
<!-- ✅ -->
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />

<!-- ❌ -->
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, user-scalable=no" />
```

## Testing

Run axe-core in CI and dev:

```bash
npm install --save-dev @axe-core/playwright
```

```ts
// playwright/a11y.spec.ts
import { checkA11y } from 'axe-playwright';

test('home page has no a11y violations', async ({ page }) => {
  await page.goto('/');
  await checkA11y(page, undefined, {
    detailedReport: true,
    runOnly: { type: 'tag', values: ['wcag2a', 'wcag2aa'] },
  });
});
```

Manual checks before every ship:
- Tab through the full page — every action reachable?
- Screen reader (VoiceOver on Mac, NVDA on Windows) — does it make sense?
- Zoom to 200% — does layout break?
- Color-blind simulation in Chrome DevTools.

## Pre-Ship Accessibility Checklist

```markdown
- [ ] All interactive elements reachable by keyboard
- [ ] Focus ring visible on all interactive elements
- [ ] Color contrast ≥ 4.5:1 for body text (light and dark)
- [ ] All images have alt text (or alt="" if decorative)
- [ ] All form inputs have associated labels
- [ ] Dynamic regions use aria-live or role="status"
- [ ] Error messages use role="alert"
- [ ] No user-scalable=no in viewport meta
- [ ] Touch targets ≥ 44×44px
- [ ] axe-core passes in CI or dev run
```
